---
/**
 * The thesis. Two columns on wide screens, one on narrow; each block rises
 * into view as it scrolls in, driven by the scroll position where the
 * browser supports view timelines and simply visible everywhere else.
 */
---

<section class="thesis" aria-labelledby="thesis-title">
	<h2 id="thesis-title" class="thesis__title reveal">
		The hard part is everything around the model.
	</h2>
	<p class="thesis__body reveal">
		Current models can do most of what people ask of them. In practice they disappoint, because
		nobody told them what the work was. What a person wants is usually clear in their head and
		incomplete on the page, and a model only ever sees the page. Deciding what it is shown and
		what it is allowed to change closes that gap one edge at a time. That is the part we work
		on.
	</p>
</section>

<style>
	.thesis {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 340px), 1fr));
		gap: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 4.5rem);
		align-items: start;
		padding: var(--section-block) var(--gutter);
		border-block-start: var(--rule);
	}

	.thesis__title {
		font-size: var(--text-title);
	}

	.thesis__body {
		max-inline-size: 34em;
		font-size: clamp(1.125rem, 1.3vw, 1.3125rem);
		line-height: 1.55;
		color: var(--color-fg-body);
	}

	@supports (animation-timeline: view()) {
		@media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference) {
			.reveal {
				animation: rise linear both;
				animation-timeline: view();
				animation-range: entry 0% entry 60%;
			}
		}
	}
</style>
